"Score each option 1-5 on each criterion. There is no NA: a field that says \"none\" or \"none known\" scores 1. Give each score a reason of at most 20 words. Score from the quantities, sources and gaps the option names; ignore verdict words such as COMPUTE-BOUND or NOT COMPUTE-BOUND. Also label each option SAME, ADJACENT or ELSEWHERE against the root question, with a reason: SAME if it asks the root question or a sub-question of it, ADJACENT if it has the root's subject but asks a different question, ELSEWHERE if its subject is different. Decide the subject from the title and summary; count root_link only if the summary itself describes the root question's object of study. Do not add up the scores. Decide only from the text below; do not use tools.
Root question: Can molecular mapping of AAV capsid-receptor interactions on brain microvascular endothelial cells determine which AAV variants transcytose across the blood-brain barrier versus remain intracellular, and for which capsid-receptor binding signatures?
Criteria:
stakes: Suppose the question this option raises were answered, either way. 5 = a choice someone faces (what to buy, build, collect or scale next) turns on the answer, and either answer would move it; 3 = the answer would refine a belief but no choice turns on it, or one answer is already much more likely than the other; 1 = either answer is already expected, or nothing would change. Do not score how famous or important the field is, or how close it is to the root question.
open: Has published work already measured how the answer changes with the quantity compute buys here (samples, ensemble members, resolution, model runs, model size, search width), across the range that $1,000 of Lambda on-demand GPU time (for scale, about 250 H100-hours) can reach? 5 = names the quantity and where published measurements stop (or that none exist), and the unmeasured range starts within that reach; 3 = the unmeasured range is reachable only through a smaller stand-in system, or published work already covers part of the reachable range; 1 = names no compute-bought quantity, or published work already covers everything within that reach, so the open range lies only beyond it.
reshape: Does the option name a part of the work that one answer waits on step after step, and a reason those steps might not have to run in order? 5 = names that chain and roughly how long it is; one answer leaves most of a GPU idle (a small state, or few runs needed, so copies side by side would not fill it); names what would have to be true of the system for the steps to be computed at the same time, in a form a cheap measurement could check; and no cited source already computes this chain in parallel for this system; 3 = names the chain and a way to restructure it, but one of these fails: the answer needs many independent runs, so copies side by side already fill the hardware; one run already fills a GPU; or no checkable condition is named; 1 = sequential says none, or the only parallelism is independent pieces (copies, a sweep, one job per GPU), or a cited source already computes this chain in parallel for this system. A method published for a different system does not lower this score. Do not score how famous the method or field is.
Options, one per line:
{\"id\":\"O\",\"title\":\"Exhaustive capsid–receptor complex enumeration (docking and AlphaFold-Multimer)\",\"summary\":\"Enumerate binding modes of engineered capsid libraries against the BBB receptor panel (LY6A, LY6C1, ALPL, LRP6, CA4, AAVR) with docking, MD refinement, and AlphaFold-Multimer to test whether transcytosis-competent pairs share a geometric motif such as 3-fold-axis engagement of GPI-anchored receptors (https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_2024_FINAL_Ishan.pdf). Published modeling covers only single-digit complexes, e.g. AlphaFold-Multimer models of LRP6 with AAV-X1 and CAP-Mac VR-VIII peptides (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518), against an experimental catalog of ~150 AAV capsid structures (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079). Narrowing: This leaves aside everything after binding — endosomal sorting, lysosomal degradation, nuclear import — so the computed interface geometry stands in for the binding step alone, not for fate. Its answer still moves the root question because it either widens or closes the catalog of candidate signatures (Q3) against which the sufficiency claim (Q1) must be tested.\",\"root_link\":\"Bears on Q3 of the root question — for which capsid–receptor binding signatures transcytosis occurs — specifically whether a shared interface motif marks transcytosis-competent complexes.\",\"compute_open\":\"More parallel compute would buy model runs (capsid × receptor × pose); published measurements of its effect stop at single-digit numbers of AAV–receptor complexes modeled per study — two LRP6 peptide complexes in https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518 — and above that it is unknown whether exhaustive enumeration would surface a shared transcytosis-competent motif or demonstrate that no such motif exists.\",\"sequential\":\"none: every capsid–receptor pair is an independent docking or AlphaFold-Multimer job with its own random seeds, so the work already splits into independent pieces.\"}
{\"id\":\"V1\",\"title\":\"Full-capsid, membrane-anchored receptor enumeration of the 3-fold GPI engagement motif\",\"summary\":\"Enumerate binding modes of the full 60-mer capsid at the 3-fold spike against membrane-embedded, GPI-anchored LY6A and the rest of the BBB receptor panel (LY6C1, ALPL, LRP6, CA4, AAVR) with docking, MD refinement and AlphaFold-Multimer, rather than against the isolated VR-VIII peptide (AA587–594) used in APPRAISE-style competition modeling. Anchor the sweep on the published PHP.eB–LY6A complex (PDB 7WQO) rebuilt with its GPI anchor and a lipid-bilayer patch, and test whether transcytosis-competent pairs share a 3-fold-axis anchor geometry that non-cognate pairs lack. Published modeling covers only peptide-scale complexes, e.g. AlphaFold-Multimer models of LRP6 with AAV-X1 and CAP-Mac VR-VIII peptides (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518), so whether the motif survives a whole-capsid, membrane-proximal representation is untested.\",\"root_link\":\"Bears on Q3 of the root question — which capsid–receptor binding signatures permit transcytosis — by asking whether the shared 3-fold-axis GPI-engagement motif is a property of the intact capsid engaging a membrane receptor rather than of peptide competition.\",\"compute_open\":\"More parallel compute buys full-capsid × receptor × pose jobs, which are far more expensive per model than peptide jobs; published measurements of depth effects stop at single-digit peptide complexes per study, and above that it is unknown whether whole-capsid sampling preserves, sharpens or dissolves the shared-motif call.\",\"sequential\":\"none: every full-capsid–receptor pose is an independent docking or AlphaFold-Multimer job with its own random seeds.\"}
{\"id\":\"V2\",\"title\":\"Motif call judged against matched human Transwell transcytosis labels on conserved ALPL\",\"summary\":\"Enumerate binding modes of engineered capsid libraries against the BBB receptor panel (LY6A, LY6C1, ALPL, LRP6, CA4, AAVR) with docking, MD refinement and AlphaFold-Multimer, but judge the competent-minus-retained motif gap against per-pair transcytose-versus-retain labels measured in a human polarized barrier (Transwell) assay for ALPL, the conserved panel receptor, anchored on Voyager's VCAP-102 ± ALPL versus AAV9 result. Keep the published PHP.eB–LY6A complex as the structural control for the pose rebuild, and score the motif only on pairs that carry a direct human transcytosis measurement rather than on mixed-species in vivo transduction. Published modeling covers single-digit complexes, and the only published Transwell comparison is VCAP-102/ALPL against AAV9 (https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_2024_FINAL_Ishan.pdf).\",\"root_link\":\"Bears on Q1 and Q3 of the root question — whether a binding signature is sufficient for transcytosis — by asking whether the 3-fold-axis GPI-engagement gap separates transcytosis-competent from retained pairs when labels come from human endothelium and a conserved receptor.\",\"compute_open\":\"More parallel compute buys pose models across the expanded, label-matched ALPL pair set (72 pairs at 144, 720 and 2,880 models); previously only a single transcytosis pair existed to compare against, so whether a motif emerges once labels are measured in the same human assay is unknown.\",\"sequential\":\"none: each capsid–receptor pose is an independent docking or AlphaFold-Multimer job, and the Transwell measurements are a separate bench block that does not gate the pose sweep.\"}
{\"id\":\"V3\",\"title\":\"Motif calls emitted for Capsida NR001–NR005 and Lir Starfish binding-assay readouts\",\"summary\":\"Enumerate binding modes of capsid libraries against the human BBB-receptor set used by Capsida's NR001–NR005 platform and Lir's Starfish capsid-structure pipeline (ALPL, AAVR, LRP6 and their panel partners) with docking, MD refinement and AlphaFold-Multimer, emitting calls in the format of plate- and bead-based capsid–receptor binding assays. Score whether 3-fold-axis engagement geometry agrees with measured bind/no-bind receptor by receptor, then rank the binding-positive pairs as the only candidates worth a transcytosis claim. Published modeling covers only single-digit complexes, and neither Capsida's nor Lir's structural pipeline has been assessed against exhaustive enumeration.\",\"root_link\":\"Bears on Q3 of the root question — which capsid–receptor binding signatures are candidates for transcytosis — by pruning the catalog to pairs that survive a real human-receptor binding assay before any transcytosis claim (Q1) is attempted.\",\"compute_open\":\"More parallel compute buys model runs across capsid × receptor × pose for the NR001–NR005 receptor set, letting the shared-motif question be tested receptor by receptor against binding readouts rather than at a single receptor; published depth effects stop at single-digit complexes and the proprietary pipelines are unmeasured, so the payoff is unknown.\",\"sequential\":\"none: each capsid–receptor pose is an independent docking or AlphaFold-Multimer job with its own seeds, and the plate/bead binding readouts are a separate block.\"}

